# Binary assets. These MUST never be treated as text: a raw RGB565 raster is
# full of 0x0D and 0x0A bytes that mean pixel data, not line endings, and a
# CRLF rewrite would corrupt the image and desync the exact 411,640-byte size
# src/background.cpp checks before loading it. Git for Windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM config, where it is invisible to
# `git config --global --list`, so this is not hypothetical.
#
# `binary` is shorthand for `-diff -merge -text`: never converted, never
# line-diffed, never auto-merged.
*.rgb565 binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.bmp    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.bin    binary

